1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:03,533
What if all shadows vanished at noon, except one?

2
00:00:03,573 --> 00:00:05,906
The sun reaches the top of the sky.

3
00:00:05,946 --> 00:00:08,280
Every shadow on the street shrinks,

4
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:10,924
flickers, and pops, like a soap bubble.

5
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,701
People gasp, then shrug.

6
00:00:13,741 --> 00:00:15,359
Hot sidewalks get hotter,

7
00:00:15,399 --> 00:00:17,347
and picnic blankets need hats.

8
00:00:17,387 --> 00:00:19,403
But in the middle of the plaza,

9
00:00:19,443 --> 00:00:21,259
one single shadow stays put,

10
00:00:21,299 --> 00:00:23,181
sharp as ink, and it's yours.

11
00:00:24,450 --> 00:00:27,858
Within minutes, the whole town is crowding around you.

12
00:00:27,898 --> 00:00:30,348
Everyone is hot, and your shadow is the

13
00:00:30,388 --> 00:00:31,625
only shade on Earth.

14
00:00:31,665 --> 00:00:34,817
Soon forty neighbors are squished beneath a shadow

15
00:00:34,857 --> 00:00:35,839
shaped like you.

16
00:00:37,150 --> 00:00:39,930
Scientists would say shadows can't just disappear,

17
00:00:39,970 --> 00:00:42,298
because they're only the absence of light.

18
00:00:42,338 --> 00:00:43,821
In this thought experiment,

19
00:00:43,861 --> 00:00:46,753
the missing shade feels like missing a quiet friend.

20
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:48,746
Mayors panic.

21
00:00:48,786 --> 00:00:50,805
Newspapers write headlines like,

22
00:00:50,845 --> 00:00:52,606
one shadow to rule them all.

23
00:00:52,646 --> 00:00:54,600
You just want to buy ice cream,

24
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:58,267
but your shadow keeps tugging you gently down the street.

25
00:00:59,450 --> 00:01:01,942
The shadow finally stops at an empty lot

26
00:01:01,982 --> 00:01:03,207
where nothing grows.

27
00:01:03,247 --> 00:01:07,321
It stretches, wriggles, and settles into a perfect little circle.

28
00:01:07,361 --> 00:01:09,410
Then it waits, patient as a seed.

29
00:01:10,650 --> 00:01:11,927
Here is the twist.

30
00:01:11,967 --> 00:01:14,926
A tiny green sprout pushes up through the

31
00:01:14,966 --> 00:01:16,462
middle of the shadow.

32
00:01:16,502 --> 00:01:18,291
It was never your shadow.

33
00:01:18,331 --> 00:01:20,778
It was the shadow of the tree this

34
00:01:20,818 --> 00:01:22,753
seed would become, one day.

35
00:01:24,050 --> 00:01:26,470
So the whole town waters the sprout.

36
00:01:26,510 --> 00:01:28,111
Years later it's a huge,

37
00:01:28,151 --> 00:01:30,844
leafy tree with a shadow wide enough for

38
00:01:30,884 --> 00:01:32,553
everyone, and every noon,

39
00:01:32,593 --> 00:01:35,081
the shadows return to sit beneath it.
